# Hold the NVIDIA 595-server userspace at the version of the CC kernel
# modules that actually load (the signed bundle from the cvm-images kernel-v*
# release, nvidia-cc-bundle-signed-595.71.05-6.17.0-35-generic). libcuda,
# nvidia-smi and the firmware must match the loaded module exactly, or the
# GPU never comes up.
#
# Why a pin, when Mirror= is a dated snapshot: mkosi still adds
# security.ubuntu.com noble-security unsnapshotted, and 595.91.07 landed there
# after tdx-gpu-v0.6.59. apt then wanted 595.91.07 userspace beside the
# snapshot's linux-modules-nvidia-595-server-open-6.17.0-35-generic, which
# requires <= 595.71.05, and the image build failed.
#
# When cvm-images ships a bundle for a newer driver, bump this with it.
Package: *nvidia*-595-server*
Pin: version 595.71.05*
Pin-Priority: 1001
